Performance Bottlenecks Identified & Solved
1. Why scrolling felt laggy
Over 100 uncontained avatar elements: The editor loaded 100+ avatar buttons and images inside nested horizontal scrollers without CSS layout containment. During vertical scrolling, the browser's rendering engine had to continuously calculate layout and repaint all off-screen items on the CPU.
Lack of GPU scroll compositing: Scrolling containers did not utilize hardware compositing layers (transform: translateZ(0), will-change: scroll-position, -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch), causing frame drops during scroll.
Fix: Added .smooth-scroll, .avatar-scroll-container (contain: content), and .cv-auto (content-visibility: auto) in index.html, allowing the browser to skip layout and paint work for off-screen sections until they enter the viewport.
2. Why selecting a card design had a delay
Handler Churn & Failed Component Memoization: In App.tsx, callbacks like handleInputChange, handleGenerateSample, and handleAutoTrigger recreated their function references on every render because they listed studentInfo and template in their dependency arrays. This invalidated React.memo(EditorPanel), causing the entire form (all 12 inputs, 12 template buttons, country buttons, and 100 avatar images) to re-render synchronously.
Monolithic Template Switching: Clicking a template triggered synchronous unmounting, remounting, and repainting of both Front and Back cards simultaneously on the main thread.
Keystroke Loop Overheads: Every keystroke in the university field ran an O(N × M) scan across thousands of school strings to detect country matching.
Key Optimizations Applied
Stable Handlers with React Refs (App.tsx):
Replaced state dependencies in callbacks with live refs (studentInfoRef, templateRef, isNameLockedRef, isDateLockedRef). Handlers now maintain persistent identities, keeping EditorPanel and PreviewPanel truly memoized.
Snappy Template Selection with React.startTransition:
Wrapped template switching in React.startTransition. The active button updates immediately (0ms delay), while card layout adaptation is scheduled cooperatively without freezing the main thread.
Extracted memoized TemplateButton components so only the newly selected and previously selected template buttons re-render upon selection instead of all 12.
Micro-Memoized Avatar Picker (EditorPanel.tsx):
Extracted AvatarItem with React.memo. Selecting an avatar now only re-renders the 2 affected items (the previous and new selection), avoiding recalculation of the remaining 99+ avatars.
Targeted Prop Equality Comparator on IdCard:
Implemented areIdCardPropsEqual on IdCard and memoized template components so cards only re-render when visible card data actually changes, avoiding expensive SVG and barcode re-renders.
O(1) Precomputed Country Lookup & Memoized Options:
Created a module-level SCHOOL_TO_COUNTRY_MAP for instant O(1) country synchronization and memoized currentSchools options.
Memoized InputField:
Wrapped InputField in React.memo, preventing all 12 input components from re-rendering whenever text is typed in a single field.
